# Observability & Errors

- Structured JSON logs (Pino). Include correlation fields (`connection_id`, upgrade outcome) without secrets.
- **Always redact**: raw tickets, query strings containing `ticket=`, Sanctum tokens, session cookies, emails, Authorization headers, Redis key payloads with PII.
- Client-facing errors use stable codes (`TICKET_INVALID`, `ORIGIN_REJECTED`, `REDIS_UNAVAILABLE`, `PROTOCOL_UNSUPPORTED`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE`, `SHUTTING_DOWN`). Never leak stack traces or internal topology to clients.
- `GET /health/live` = process up. `GET /health/ready` = Redis ticket path operational. Ready fails closed on Redis outage; live may still return 200.
- Graceful shutdown on SIGTERM/SIGINT: stop accepting upgrades, close sockets with a deadline, disconnect Redis, exit. Log lifecycle without credentials.
- Prefer measurable counters for connections accepted/rejected and heartbeat timeouts when adding metrics later.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
logger.info({ url: req.url }, "upgrade"); // leaks ticket

// ✅ GOOD
logger.info({ path: "/ws", outcome: "accepted", connectionId }, "upgrade");
```
